      ["nutrition.body_composition.hunger", "Hunger", "the drive to eat, 0 to 1: rises with hours since the last meal (0.05/h) and with the energy deficit (+0.1 per 500 kcal below the day's need); falls with fullness (x(1 - fullness)); starvation stage 2+ holds it at 1.0; a fever or seasickness lowers it (x0.5) even when the body needs food", "index", "proposed (Rex's go-ahead 2026-10-29)", "open"],
      ["nutrition.body_composition.appetite", "Appetite", "the wish to eat this food now, 0 to 1 per meal offered: hunger x palatability x state. Palatability: a hot meal 1.0, fresh meat 1.0, biscuit and salt horse for the 30th day 0.6, spoiled food 0.3, a favourite 1.2, a hated one 0.5 (per character, the story keeper's); raised by the cook's skill (STATS Cooking: +0.1 at 30, +0.3 at 70; the skilled cook makes the same stores eaten, so consumption, mood and hearts toward the cook follow: ChatGPT's point, agreed). State: fever x0.3, drunk x0.7, seasick x0.2, grief x0.6. A man full but wanting pudding is appetite over fullness; a man hungry but off his food is hunger without appetite", "index", "proposed (Rex's go-ahead 2026-10-29)", "open"],
      ["nutrition.body_composition.eating-rule", "Eating rule", "a crew mate eats the meal if appetite over 0.3, or if hunger over 0.8 whatever the appetite; what is eaten fills fullness and intake; what is refused goes back to the stores or over the side", "rule", "proposed (Rex's go-ahead 2026-10-29)", "open"],
      ["nutrition.body_composition.starvation-stages", "Starvation stages", "day 1 glycogen gone; days 2 to 7 ketosis, work capacity x0.8; weeks 2 to 6 wasting, x0.5, immune weak; death when fat is gone or mass under 60% of start", "-", "proposed", "open"]
